{
  "title": "Namaz of Holy Prophet(s)",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "After concluding the two units of prayer, say the following supplication:\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ رَبُّنَا وَ رَبُّ اٰبَآئِنَا الْاَوَّلِيْنَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU RABBUNAA WA RABBU AABAAA'INAL AWWALEEN\nThere is no god save Allah, our Lord and the Lord of our forefathers.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ اِلٰهًا وَاحِدًا وَّ نَحْنُ لَهٗ مُسْلِمُوْنَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU ILAAHAN WAAHIDAN WA NAHNU LAHOO MUSLIMOON\nThere is no god save Allah, One God, and unto Him we submit.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ لَا نَعْبُدُ اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ وَ لَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU LAA NA'BUDU ILLAA IYYAAHU MUKHLISEENA LAHUD DEENA WA LAW KARIHAL MUSHRIKOON\nThere is no god save Allah; we worship none save Him, being sincere to Him in religion, though the polytheists be averse.",
  "merits": "Sayyid Ibn Tawus narrates that Imam al-Rida (a.s.) was asked about the prayer of the Holy Prophet (s). He described it as two units: in each unit recite Surah al-Fatihah once and Surah al-Qadr fifteen times. In ruku' recite it fifteen times, upon rising fifteen times, in the first sajdah fifteen times, between sajdahs fifteen times, in the second sajdah fifteen times, and upon rising before the next unit fifteen times."
}
